.TH "tm" "1" "2026\-11\-08"
.PP
.SH NAME
tm \- universal taskmark utility
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtm\fR <command> [options]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBtm\fR is the command\-line interface for SPEC\-TASKMARK\-04 taskmark files.\& It
provides subcommands for atomic task mutations, compact task listings with
ephemeral hex handles, sweeping completed tasks between task documents in
strict reverse chronological order, archiving aged\-out sections, validating
files for spec compliance, and filtering arbitrary text into and out of a
payload block.\& The specification it implements is documented in
\fIdoc/taskmark_spec.\&md\fR.\&
.PP
Unless a path is given, \fBtm\fR operates on the \fI.\&tasks\fR directory relative to
the current working directory (the layout described by the spec).\&
.PP
.SH COMMANDS
\fBinit\fR [\-\-orphan [\fIBRANCH\fR]] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR]
.RS 4
Bootstrap \fI.\&tasks\fR with starter \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR, \fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR, and
\fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR files.\& Never overwrites a file that already exists.\&
With \fB\-\-orphan\fR, keeps the tasks directory on its own git branch,
mounted as a worktree (see \fB\-\-orphan\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBsync\fR [\-m \fIMSG\fR] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR] [\-p|\-\-push]
.RS 4
Stage and commit every change in the tasks directory (default message
"tasks: sync (<timestamp>)"), and with \fB\-\-push\fR push it.\& The tasks
directory must be the top level of its own git work tree \-\- normally
the worktree made by \fBinit \-\-orphan\fR \-\- so nothing outside it can be
staged; a plain directory inside a larger repository is refused.\& Git
hooks run as for any commit, and git'\&s own messages are shown when a
commit or push fails.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBlist\fR [\-\-pending|\-\-all] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR] [\fIfile\fR.\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Print one line per task, its handle and summary, e.\&g.\&
"[f4a1] (A) Task text", without payload blocks, to keep listings short
for humans and AI agents alike.\& By default, lists pending tasks from the
active task document.\& With \fB\-\-all\fR, lists both pending and completed
tasks (completed tasks marked `[x]`).\& Given several files, each listing
is headed `== <file>`.\& A file with nothing to list prints nothing on
standard output and a short note on standard error.\& A missing file is
an error.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBadd\fR \fI<task\-text>\fR [\-p|\-\-priority \fIPRI\fR] [\-\-section \fISECTION\fR] [\-\-file \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR]
.RS 4
Add a pending task at the end of the named section'\&s own content
(before its first subheading), or of the first heading'\&s when no
\fB\-\-section\fR is given.\& An unknown section or a missing file is an error;
no file is ever created.\& \fB\-p A\fR adds the `(A)` priority flag.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdone\fR \fI<hash\-or\-pattern>\fR [\-\-git [\fIREV\fR]] [\-\-file \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR]
.RS 4
Find a pending task in \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR (or \fB\-\-file\fR) by handle or
substring (see TASK HANDLES), mark it `\- [x]` in place, and stamp a
Completed field with the local date into the leading run of its
labeled fields, adding `git:<sha>` with \fB\-\-git\fR.\& Only pending tasks are
candidates; a match that is already completed is reported as such.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBmove\fR \fI<hash\-or\-pattern>\fR [\-\-from \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-to \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-section \fISECTION\fR] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR]
.RS 4
Move a task and its payload from one file to another (by default from
\fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR to \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR), or to another section of the same
file, placed as for \fBadd\fR.\& The destination is written before the task
is removed from the source, so an interrupted move leaves a duplicate,
never a loss.\& The destination must exist.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBsweep\fR
.RS 4
Move every `\- [x]` task and its payload out of \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR and into
\fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR, bucketed under a "## YYYY\-MM" section for the month
of the sweep, or "## Sprint \fILABEL\fR" with \fB\-\-sprint\fR.\& Tasks within a
section and sections within the file are kept in strict reverse chronological
order (newest completed first).\& Headings and top\-level prose in \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR
are never swept, even when every task beneath them is done.\& \fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR
is never read or written.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBarchive\fR
.RS 4
Move sections aged out of \fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR into
\fI.\&tasks/archive/<YYYY>/<YYYY\-MM>.\&tm.\&md\fR, grouped by the month of
each section'\&s most recent \fBCompleted\fR task and inserted newest first
beneath the archive file'\&s title.\& A section is retained if it is among
the 2 newest or its most recent \fBCompleted\fR task is dated within the
last 14 days.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBvalidate\fR [\-\-fix] [file.\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Validate taskmark file(s) for SPEC\-TASKMARK\-04 compliance.\& If no \fIfile\fR
is given, defaults to the configured active file.\& If \fB\-\-fix\fR is given,
automatically repairs common formatting errors (over\-indented bullet
continuations and sub\-lists, wrapped labeled fields, missing blank lines
after labeled fields, prose directly beneath a task or payload, hard
tabs, leading frontmatter blocks from pre\-0.\&4 files, and top\-level dash
bullets converted to '\&*'\&).\& The file'\&s newline style is preserved.\& Exits 0 on success (or successful
repair), 1 on validation failure or file error.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBindent\fR [info]
.RS 4
Read stdin, prefix every non\-blank line with the four\-space payload
indent, and write the result to stdout.\& Blank lines are emitted
genuinely empty.\& \fIinfo\fR, if given, wraps the result in a fenced code
block carrying that info string.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdedent\fR [\-\-fence]
.RS 4
Read stdin, remove exactly four leading spaces from every non\-blank
line, and write the result to stdout.\& Exits non\-zero rather than
truncate a line that lacks the full four\-space prefix.\& \fB\-\-fence\fR also
drops the first and last line, for lifting a fenced block back out.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBhelp\fR
.RS 4
Show a short usage summary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBversion\fR
.RS 4
Print the version and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
\fB\-\-pending\fR
.RS 4
With \fBlist\fR: output only pending tasks (the default).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-all\fR
.RS 4
With \fBlist\fR: output both pending and completed tasks.\& Completed tasks are
marked with `[x]`.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-priority\fR \fIPRI\fR
.RS 4
With \fBadd\fR: assign a priority flag `(A)`\-`(Z)` to the task.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-section\fR \fISECTION\fR
.RS 4
With \fBadd\fR and \fBmove\fR: heading (matched case\-insensitively) whose own
content the task is appended to.\& Must exist.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Target file to operate on.\& Defaults to the configured active file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-from\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
With \fBmove\fR: source file to move the task from (defaults to \fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-to\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
With \fBmove\fR: destination file to move the task to (defaults to \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-git\fR [\fIREV\fR]
.RS 4
With \fBdone\fR: record the short SHA of \fIREV\fR (default \fBHEAD\fR) in the
Completed field, e.\&g.\& `> \fB\fRCompleted:\fB\fR YYYY\-MM\-DD git:<sha>`.\& \fIREV\fR
must name a commit in the current repository.\& The word after \fB\-\-git\fR is
taken as \fIREV\fR only when the command would otherwise have two
arguments, so `tm done \-\-git abc1234 parser` and `tm done parser \-\-git`
both work; `\-\-git=`\fIREV\fR is always unambiguous.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-sprint\fR \fILABEL\fR
.RS 4
With \fBsweep\fR: bucket the swept tasks under "## Sprint \fILABEL\fR" instead
of the current month.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Report what would move and change nothing.\& Applies to \fBsweep\fR and
\fBarchive\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-tasks\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Directory holding the task files.\& Defaults to \fI.\&/.\&tasks\fR, or the
\fBtasks_dir\fR set in \fI.\&taskmarkrc\fR (see CONFIGURATION).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-orphan\fR [\fIBRANCH\fR]
.RS 4
With \fBinit\fR, run from the repository root: mount branch \fIBRANCH\fR
(default \fItasks\fR) at the tasks directory as a git worktree, add the
directory to \fI.\&gitignore\fR, and set \fBtasks_dir\fR in \fI.\&taskmarkrc\fR.\& An
existing local branch is mounted as is; a branch already fetched from a
remote is checked out tracking it, so a collaborator joins the shared
task history; otherwise a new orphan branch is created with only the
starter files, committed with hooks running.\& Works with any git that has
\fBgit worktree\fR.\& Refuses an existing directory that is not a worktree.\&
The changed \fI.\&gitignore\fR and \fI.\&taskmarkrc\fR are left for you to commit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-message\fR \fIMSG\fR
.RS 4
With \fBsync\fR: commit message, passed to git verbatim.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-push\fR
.RS 4
With \fBsync\fR: push after committing.\& The first push of a new branch sets
its upstream to \fIorigin\fR, or to the only remote.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Show help for the command.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH TASK HANDLES
Task files carry no IDs or numbering.\& Instead \fBtm\fR derives a deterministic
8\-hex\-digit hash from each task'\&s summary (the task line minus its checkbox
and outer whitespace, so it survives \fBtm done\fR), and shows its shortest
prefix of at least 4 digits that is unique within the file as the task'\&s
\fIhandle\fR, e.\&g.\& `[f4a1]`.\& Editing a task'\&s text changes its handle.\&
.PP
\fBdone\fR and \fBmove\fR accept:
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
A handle, or any longer prefix of the same hash, with or without
brackets.\& A prefix shared by several tasks is rejected, listing each
candidate with its own unique handle.\&
.IP \(bu 4
Otherwise, a case\-insensitive substring of the task summary.\& A substring
matching several tasks is likewise rejected with the candidates listed.\&
.PD
.PP
Two tasks with identical summaries share a hash; make their text differ to
address them separately.\&
.PP
For \fBadd\fR, \fBdone\fR, \fBmove\fR, and \fBlist\fR, `\-\-` ends the options, so task text or
a pattern may begin with '\&\-'\&: `tm add \-\- "\-v flag handling"`.\&
.PP
Task files may be symlinks: \fBtm\fR writes through a link to its target and
leaves the link in place.\&
.PP
.SH FILES
\fI.\&tasks/active.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
The current sprint.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI.\&tasks/future.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
Planned work not yet scheduled to a sprint.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI.\&tasks/completed.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
Strict reverse\-chronological archive of completed work, newest first.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI.\&tasks/archive/<YYYY>/<YYYY\-MM>.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
Sections aged out of \fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR, newest first.\& Tool\-managed;
never hand\-authored.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI<tasks\-dir>/.\&tm.\&lock\fR
.RS 4
Transient lock directory held by \fBadd\fR, \fBdone\fR, \fBmove\fR, \fBsweep\fR,
\fBarchive\fR, and \fBvalidate \-\-fix\fR for the duration of their read\-modify\-write,
so concurrent \fBtm\fR runs wait for each other instead of losing updates.\&
A stale lock left by a killed process may be removed by hand.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration uses a flat `key: value` format, read from two locations, each
optional:
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBGlobal\fR — \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taskmark/config\fR, falling back to
\fI\(ti/.\&config/taskmark/config\fR when unset.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBLocal\fR — \fI.\&taskmarkrc\fR in the directory \fBtm\fR is invoked from.\&
.PD
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
tasks_dir: \&.tasks
active_file: active\&.tm\&.md
future_file: future\&.tm\&.md
completed_file: completed\&.tm\&.md
archive_dir: archive
.fi
.RE
.PP
Resolution is per key, highest priority first: an explicit command\-line
option, the local file, the global file, then the built\-in default shown
above.\& When \fBtasks_dir\fR is not set anywhere and \fI.\&/.\&tasks\fR does not
exist but \fI.\&/doc/tasks\fR (the pre\-0.\&4 default) does, \fI.\&/doc/tasks\fR is used.\&
An absent file, an absent key, or an unparseable line falls back
silently to the next source.\& See \fIdoc/taskmark_spec.\&md\fR §9 for the full
resolution order.\&
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
\fIdoc/taskmark_spec.\&md\fR
.RS 4
The SPEC\-TASKMARK\-04 specification implemented by this tool.\&
.RE
